## Bug 1: forward --no-meta, --filter-prog, --fs-events from `mise watch` to watchexec

Prototype patch against `https://github.com/jdx/mise.git` HEAD `70c2f0ba06bca99417d3f0e416ef0363ec91bf2e`
(`v2026.5.11-1-g70c2f0b`). Applies cleanly with `git apply` from the mise repo root.

```diff
diff --git a/src/cli/watch.rs b/src/cli/watch.rs
index f66a665..a87a01b 100644
--- a/src/cli/watch.rs
+++ b/src/cli/watch.rs
@@ -176,6 +176,39 @@ impl Watch {
                 args.push(pattern.to_string());
             }
         }
+        if self.watchexec.filter_fs_meta {
+            args.push("--no-meta".to_string());
+        }
+        // Forward --fs-events only when the user picked a non-default set.
+        // The clap default (create,remove,rename,modify,metadata) matches
+        // watchexec's own default, so an unset --fs-events is identical to
+        // omitting the flag. Forwarding the default unconditionally would
+        // also conflict with watchexec's `--no-meta` because both ship
+        // event-filter state.
+        if !self.watchexec.filter_fs_events.is_empty()
+            && self.watchexec.filter_fs_events.as_slice() != DEFAULT_FS_EVENTS
+        {
+            args.push("--fs-events".to_string());
+            args.push(
+                self.watchexec
+                    .filter_fs_events
+                    .iter()
+                    .map(|e| {
+                        e.to_possible_value()
+                            .expect("FsEvent variants all have ValueEnum names")
+                            .get_name()
+                            .to_string()
+                    })
+                    .collect::<Vec<_>>()
+                    .join(","),
+            );
+        }
+        if !self.watchexec.filter_programs.is_empty() {
+            for prog in &self.watchexec.filter_programs {
+                args.push("--filter-prog".to_string());
+                args.push(prog.clone());
+            }
+        }
         if let Some(watch_file) = &self.watchexec.watch_file {
             args.push("--watch-file".to_string());
             args.push(watch_file.to_string_lossy().to_string());
@@ -1238,6 +1271,17 @@ pub enum FsEvent {
     Metadata,
 }

+/// Mirror of the `--fs-events` clap default. Kept in sync with the
+/// `default_value` on `WatchexecArgs::filter_fs_events` so the forward path
+/// can recognise an unchanged value and omit the flag.
+const DEFAULT_FS_EVENTS: &[FsEvent] = &[
+    FsEvent::Create,
+    FsEvent::Remove,
+    FsEvent::Rename,
+    FsEvent::Modify,
+    FsEvent::Metadata,
+];
+
 #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Eq, PartialEq, ValueEnum)]
 #[clap(rename_all = "lower")]
 pub enum ShellCompletion {
```

Mise advertises `-J` as its CLI-facing alias because lowercase `-j` is mise's own `--jobs`
flag. The patch emits the long form `--filter-prog` to the subprocess (unambiguous and
accepted by watchexec), so no `-J` to `-j` translation is needed.

Forwarding is gated for `--fs-events`: the clap default
`create,remove,rename,modify,metadata` matches watchexec's own default, so passing it
unconditionally would add redundant noise (and would collide with `--no-meta` when both
defaults are populated by clap).

`cargo test --release -p mise` (filtered to `cli::watch`): 4/4 pass post-patch
(`merge_dedupes_across_tasks`, `merge_does_not_let_one_task_exclude_anothers_include`,
`merge_single_task_splits_pos_and_neg`, `merge_unescapes_literal_bang`).
Full mise binary unit suite (`cargo test --release -p mise --bins`): 956/956 pass.
